nd expert ratings.", "Incumbent Aaron Bean (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Aaron Bean, the Republican incumbent in this northeast Florida district, is seeking a second full term against Democrat LaShonda Holloway, who emerged from a contested primary in August. The seat leans Republican by about five points on recent partisan performance, and Bean enters the fall with roughly $1.6 million on hand compared with about $24,000 for Holloway.\n\nNo general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals and expert assessments. Every major rater places the race in the Republican-favored column, most calling it Solid or Safe R, and prediction markets price Bean's chances near 86 percent. Holloway has drawn some notable endorsements, but the resource and structural gaps make an upset a long shot.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0948, "margin": -8.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0811, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0937, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0773, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0859, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0659, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -10.0}]}